c. curative; and
d. rehabilitative.
(2) Health rehabilitation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted comprehensively, accessible 24 (twenty-four) hours, with quality and conducted in accordance with health service standards.
(15) (3) Women and children victims of acts of violence and children in conflict with the law have the right to health services free of charge, including:
a. medical services;
b. medicolegal services;
c. psychosocial counseling; and
d. visum.
(4) Further provisions regarding procedures for implementation of health services as referred to in paragraph (3) shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

